WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:02.840
We have some amazing news for you!

00:00:02.960 --> 00:00:06.600
Don’t Memorise is awarded the diamond play button!

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:10.020
Sorry, that’s fake news!

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.500
We go through news on various platforms everyday,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.440
be it in digital or printed formats.

00:00:16.820 --> 00:00:20.900
But, there’s this one question that always ponders in our minds.

00:00:21.220 --> 00:00:24.360
Why is News called so?

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:27.700
Does it mean “North, East, West and South” ?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.660
Or “Notable events, Weather and Sports” ?

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.420
We’ve heard this many times, but is 'NEWS' really an acronym?

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:38.140
Let's find out.

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.920
The answer may sound quite silly.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.780
'News' just means 'new things'.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:51.620
But then why do most of us think that News is an acronym?

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:53.120
Because back in time

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.440
"News” was not really a word in the English language.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.720
'News' is derived from the Adjective 'New'.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:01.540
And in the English language,

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.360
we know that Adjectives cannot be plural.

00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.740
Consider the example, Amazing video.

00:01:11.340 --> 00:01:13.640
Can you tell me the plural of Amazing?

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:16.320
It’s definitely not Amazings.

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:19.540
So how did the word 'News' surface?

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.500
This leap from the word ‘New'

00:01:21.500 --> 00:01:25.720
to ‘News' is believed to be influenced by Old French.

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.500
In French, 'New' means 'Nouveau'.

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:30.160
But in the French language,

00:01:30.160 --> 00:01:33.560
there's also a plural form of 'Nouveau' called 'Nouvelles',

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:37.440
from which the word 'News' was derived.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.500
So now we know why 'News' is called so!

00:01:41.020 --> 00:01:45.840
It's officially designated as a word which represents “new things''.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:50.680
But how does any random set of letters get designated as a word?

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:53.780
Let’s say, we came up with a random set of letters

00:01:54.100 --> 00:01:57.600
Kyu Box which according to us represents Curiosity.

00:01:58.180 --> 00:02:01.120
So can this word get into the Dictionary?

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.420
Well, there are a few people called Lexicographers

00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:08.360
who are assigned this task of making this decision!

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:11.700
But can Lexicographers themselves finalize

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:15.020
a particular word and include it in the dictionary?

00:02:15.460 --> 00:02:17.320
No, its not that easy!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:20.035
This new set of random letters needs to

00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:25.100
undergo various tests and also pass with flying colours.

00:02:25.380 --> 00:02:27.100
And what are these tests?

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:28.940
Curious?

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:31.240
We took the first step with you,

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:34.460
but Kyu Box is for you to explore.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.160
Let us know your findings in the comment section.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:41.680
I have something interesting to share.

00:02:41.940 --> 00:02:44.980
We will be airing one bonus Qpisode at the end of the first season.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:46.700
And guess what?

00:02:47.140 --> 00:02:49.960
We will be answering a question that you have for us.

00:02:50.420 --> 00:02:52.820
Ask us your question in the comment section below,

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:55.000
and we will answer it in that Qpisode

00:02:55.500 --> 00:02:57.220
I look forward to your questions!

